t nearly impossible to form a chow. Keeping W4-W5 allows potential for W4-W5-W6 chow (2 W6 available), and keeping B6-B7-B8-B9 maintains flexibility in the Dots suit. Discarding T7 maximizes my chances of drawing tiles that complete winning patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play T7"}
